# The automated retry after a tool timeout (plan 5.17.9, M24): after a lit run
# of a leg fails, lit-legs.ps1 runs 'lit-retry.py select' on the run's xunit
# file; when every failed test is timeout-only (a timeout marker after the
# last '# executed command:' line of its failure), at most three are and lit
# exited 1 (failed tests only) after running every test, each of them runs
# again, alone, with exactly the run's parameters, -j1 and --filter=^<escaped
# name>$, into <build>/lit-results/<leg>-retry-<stem>.log and .xml. The row
# passes with a detail that starts 'retried after timeout: <names> (<logs>)'
# when every re-run passes; it fails when a re-run fails, when more than three
# tests timed out, when a failure is not timeout-only, when lit reported an
# error or when lit did not run every test (and then nothing runs again). The
# stand-in llvm-lit of Inputs/ci-legs.py plays a scenario: it reports the
# named tests of each run, timeout-only or not, in lit's output and xunit
# format. With -Leg harness:
# (a) one timeout-only failure that passes when it runs again: PASS with the
# retry detail; the re-run's response file holds the run's parameters, the
# filter and its own xunit file, and its log and xunit file exist.
# (b) the re-run times out again: FAIL, naming the re-run's log and status.
# (c) four timeout-only failures: FAIL with '4 tests timed out; re-run the leg
# on a quieter host', and no re-run. (d) a failure that is not timeout-only:
# FAIL, no re-run. (e) one of two re-runs fails: FAIL, with both re-runs
# named. (f) no xunit file: FAIL, no re-run. (g) three timeouts that pass
# again: PASS (three is the limit). (h) a timeout with a failure of another
# kind: FAIL, no re-run. (i) A leg of two runs (wsl-p3), whose first run has
# a timeout that passes again: the re-run takes run 1's paths and parameters
# and files named <leg>-retry-run1-<stem>.*, and the row joins the runs'
# details; with -Run 1 the row is 'wsl-p3 (run 1)'. (j) lit exits 2 after an
# error in tests (a test whose outcome is 'crash': lit's 'a worker process
# crashed' error, and the tests it did not run skipped in the xunit file) with
# one timeout-only failure: FAIL with 'lit reported an error, so no retry', no
# re-run and no retry file; the same xunit file with lit exit 1 (that test
# only skipped, as after --max-failures, which stops lit without an error)
# fails with 'lit did not run 2 test(s), so no retry', again without a re-run
# or a retry file; a lit error without a failed test still ends 'the xunit
# file lists no failed test, so no retry'. (k) With -Leg net-core, whose
# --filter-out excludes harness/, an excluded and an unsupported test (each a
# <skipped> element with another message than 'Skipped') do not stop the
# retry: PASS as in (a). The stand-in's own scenario (the xunit file of (a)'s
# first run) is checked with lit-retry.py select, so the scenarios mean what
# they say. timeout-retry-sh.test checks lit-legs.sh the same way.
# REQUIRES: msil-ci-pwsh

# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/ci-legs.py setup %t/build

# (a)
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/ci-legs.py scenario %t/build 'MSIL :: harness/a.test=timeout,pass' 'MSIL :: harness/b.test=pass'
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/ci-legs.py ps1 %t/build MSIL_CI_RESULTS=%t/rows-a -- -Leg harness > %t/a.log
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t/rows-a "^lit-legs\tharness\tPASS\t\d+\tretried after timeout: MSIL :: harness/a\.test \(\S+/lit-results/harness-retry-MSIL_harness_a\.test\.log\); failed 1, passed 1; lit exit 1$"
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t/build/lit-calls.log '^arg: -j1\narg: @\S+/lit-results/harness-retry-MSIL_harness_a\.test\.params\.rsp\n(rsp: --param=\S+\n)+rsp: --filter=\^MSIL :: harness/a\\\.test\$\nrsp: --xunit-xml-output=\S+/lit-results/harness-retry-MSIL_harness_a\.test\.xml\narg: \S+[/\\]msil[/\\]test[/\\]harness$'
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t/build/lit-results/harness-retry-MSIL_harness_a.test.params.rsp "^--param=msil_require_hosted=1$" "^--param=msil_pipeline=obj$" "^--param=msil_dotnet_runtime=10$"
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t/build/lit-results/harness-retry-MSIL_harness_a.test.log "^PASS: MSIL :: harness/a\.test \(1 of 1\)$"
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t/build/lit-results/harness-retry-MSIL_harness_a.test.xml "<testcase classname=\"MSIL\.harness\" name=\"a\.test\" time=\"[0-9.]+\"/>"
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t/a.log "re-run after timeout: MSIL :: harness/a\.test"
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/ci-legs.py scenario %t/build 'MSIL :: harness/a.test=timeout,pass' 'MSIL :: harness/b.test=pass'
# RUN: not %python %t/build/bin/llvm-lit.py --xunit-xml-output=%t/a-first.xml %S/.. > %t/a-first.log
# RUN: %python %S/../../../utils/ci/lit-retry.py select %t/a-first.xml > %t/a-select.log
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t/a-select.log "\AMSIL :: harness/a\.test\n\Z"

